message:
Database: Avoid a fatal error in `wpdb::load_col_info()` if the result is not set.

This resolves an error if `mysqli_num_fields()` is called before a successful SELECT-type query is performed:
{{{
mysqli_num_fields(): Argument #1 ($result) must be of type mysqli_result, false given
}}}

Developed in https://github.com/WordPress/wordpress-develop/pull/13099.

Follow-up to r21472.

Props joehorntw, akshat2802, mukesh27, rejaulalomkhan, SergeyBiryukov.
Fixes #64130.

Support random content redirects via ?random qarg

Add opt-in support for random content redirects, so that a page request with the `?random` query argument set will return a 302 redirect to a randomly selected published post.

The pool of eligible posts may be filtered with two additional query arguments:
- `random_post_type`
- `random_cat_id`

The feature may be opted into using:

{{{
add_filter( 'enable_random_content_redirect', '__return_true' );
}}}

